# REGRESSION — the alias-spelled view defect is not specific to `.get(i)`.
#
# CELL: producer arm = the trivial-getter / `Option__Ref__` provenance block
# reached by `.first()`, rather than the `.get(i)` arm. Same coordinates
# otherwise: 1-hop alias · view via alias, mutation via root · bare-local
# root · heap-forced payload · element type String.
#
# `.get()` and `.first()` record their collection provenance through
# different arms of the same producer, so a fix applied to one arm and not
# the other would leave this cell red. Measured on the pre-fix compiler:
# rc 139 SIGSEGV on both backends. Its sibling with the view spelled
# `v.first()` is rc 0 -- the same spelling discrimination.

String mk(String a, String b):
    return a + b

void main():
    Vector[String] v = []
    v.push(mk("hel", "lo"))
    Vector[String] alias = v
    String s = alias.first().unwrap()
    int i = 0
    while i < 64:
        v.push(mk("fill", "er"))
        i = i + 1
    print(s)
